WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.380 --> 00:00:09.300
Since its founding, America has enjoyed
population growth famously fueled by

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:13.019
high immigration rates. But Americans
have historically had very large

00:00:13.019 --> 00:00:17.310
families compared to other countries, as
well. But times are changing. Birth rates

00:00:17.310 --> 00:00:21.449
today have fallen to their lowest point
in history, and while birth rates have

00:00:21.449 --> 00:00:25.019
historically been connected to economic
cycles, the present decline is happening

00:00:25.019 --> 00:00:29.340
during good economic times. The causes of
the decline will be familiar for many

00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:33.270
viewers: high housing costs, less dating
and marriage, economic and social

00:00:33.270 --> 00:00:37.350
uncertainties. And even though surveys
show Americans still want big families,

00:00:37.350 --> 00:00:42.450
there are no cheap, easy solutions to fix
this problem. And unfortunately, the

00:00:42.450 --> 00:00:45.780
problem is self-reinforcing. Fewer
children means that future generations

00:00:45.780 --> 00:00:49.620
will have fewer workers serving more
people, who themselves will have less

00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:53.969
time to bear and care for children — or
retirees for that matter. Even if

00:00:53.969 --> 00:00:57.719
Americans reform housing policy, or offer
greater financial support for families,

00:00:57.719 --> 00:01:02.250
our birth rates will continue to decline,
and the fast economic growth that made

00:01:02.250 --> 00:01:06.440
America so strong in the 20th century
could vanish in the 21st. So what do you

00:01:07.380 --> 00:01:07.880
So what do you

00:01:07.890 --> 00:01:11.300
think about this? If you could go back in
time and have your life turn out any way

00:01:11.310 --> 00:01:15.060
you wanted, how many children would you like to have? Let us know in our poll.

00:01:15.060 --> 00:01:19.259
Also, let us know what other topics you'd
like our scholars to cover in 60 seconds,

00:01:19.259 --> 00:01:24.860
and be sure to like and subscribe for
more research and videos from AEI.

